# MARAI (Morrow review harness) local working state — SQLite in WAL mode.
# Not the review record: a review that gates publication must be exported into the
# pack as review.jsonl and committed. See PUBLISH.md step 4.
marai-ledger/

# Python
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.Python
.venv/
venv/

# Mutable validator output is never a release record. Sealing regenerates it
# and copies the current report into the immutable receipts/ revision.
corpus/*/validation-report.json

# Local document caches — never served, never redistributed.
# Cited sources are committed; see source-pdfs/.gitignore.
corpus/*/pdf/

# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Cloudflare Wrangler
.wrangler
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# web/ has its own .gitignore (node_modules, dist).

# Deliberately NOT ignored — these are the evidence trail, and excluding them
# turns every citation into an unverifiable claim:
#   data/evidence-ledger.json      the ledger
#   data/taxpayer-receipt.json     the UI data model
#   data/citation-audit.json       our own measured citation-fidelity counts
#   data/_extracts/                page-marked text a third party reconciles against
#   corpus/**/*.yaml               pack inputs
#   corpus/*/extracts/             pack extracts
#   corpus/*/sources.lock          source hashes
#   receipts/**                    sealed output, including manifest.json and rendered/
# data/.gitignore currently excludes data/_extracts/ and the superseded
# taxpayer-receipt.ui-v1.json; GENERALIZATION-PLAN Phase 0 item 5 requires both to be
# committed. That contradiction is in data/.gitignore, not here.
